      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{62cea1224517083b068f949b|full_name}: Use an avatar that uses the Animator Tracking Control state behaviour to put eyes into the Animation state, as opposed to Tracking, then switch to an avatar that doesn't do this (most non-VRCFT avatars).\n\nThis bug is mainly a problem when switching from an avatar that was made for face tracking to an avatar that wasn't, since VRCFT eye tracking doesn't use VRC's eye tracking OSC endpoints.\n\nThe workaround is to switch to another avatar that doesn't use the Animation state.\n\nVRCFT avatar (with FT active) -> normal avatar = stuck eyes.\n\nVRCFT avatar (with FT active) -> normal avatar -> normal avatar = eyes move as expected.\n\nOh and forgot to mention, it's the network syncing not working, you still see the eyes move client-side. (if I remember correctly, just woke up. ^^\")",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
